{"duration_api_ms":123296,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"f4d7b83d-e56a-4841-93a3-a3dcac08aa13","total_cost_usd":0.6045672,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":115980,"cache_read_input_tokens":126496,"output_tokens":11534,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":5244},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":115980,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3128,"cache_read_input_tokens":116956,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8564,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8564},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":11534,"cacheReadInputTokens":126496,"cacheCreationInputTokens":115980,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.6045672,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":5244,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":3,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"requirements\":[{\"id\":\"req-1-dhcp-server-node1\",\"requirement\":\"Configure node1 to run a DHCP server on the private network shared with node2 and node3\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"An Ansible playbook run from node4 renders a VyOS configuration script and applies it via 'sg vyattacfg -c' as the vyos user, setting eth1=10.50.50.1/24 and a Kea-backed DHCP server (shared-network LAN, subnet 10.50.50.0/24, range .100-.200, default-router/name-server options). Post-apply verification shows the config persisted in /config/config.boot, the isc-kea-dhcp4-server systemd unit active, and 'show dhcp server statistics' reporting a live 101-address pool with active leases. This was independently re-confirmed after a full node1 reboot (boot_id changed 1f48c3dd->9d3b2f29), with eth1 address, active Kea service, and saved config all present post-reboot.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-02f28ab0733f4317\",\"cmd-95ec143ddffb4996\",\"cmd-f6be1776a30541d0\",\"cmd-b14916d478034761\"]},{\"id\":\"req-2-dhcp-clients\",\"requirement\":\"Configure node2 and node3 to obtain their private-network address from node1 via DHCP rather than a static assignment\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Because Ubuntu 16.04's Python 2.7/3.5 was incompatible with ansible-core 2.20's module payloads, the executor used ansible.builtin.raw tasks to write /etc/network/interfaces.d/ens7.cfg ('iface ens7 inet dhcp') and bring the interface up via ifdown/ifup. Both nodes leased addresses from node1's pool (10.50.50.100 and 10.50.50.101 respectively) and could ping node1 and each other. The private interface (ens7) was previously unconfigured/addressless rather than statically assigned, but the resulting behavior (DHCP-sourced address from node1) matches the material requirement. Re-verified after individual reboots of node2 and node3, with the address auto-reacquired via the persisted ifupdown config and connectivity restored.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-6a4d2d56809344cb\",\"cmd-dc124de8c0fa4537\",\"cmd-1490bf3efcd94f28\",\"cmd-5b26172c155449c5\"]},{\"id\":\"req-3-ansible-implementation\",\"requirement\":\"Implement the DHCP server/client configuration using Ansible\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"A playbook.yml on node4 (the designated control node, the only host with ansible-core installed) targets a 'dhcp_server' group (node1) and a 'dhcp_clients' group (node2, node3) via an inventory.ini, and was run to completion twice (idempotently) producing the observed DHCP server and client state.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-d4f963558cd54a02\",\"cmd-455e34623eb943db\",\"cmd-6a4d2d56809344cb\",\"cmd-dc124de8c0fa4537\"]},{\"id\":\"req-4-restart-recovery-protocol\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol: pre-restart baseline, restart, changed boot identity, and recovered state on every managed node\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"All four nodes show a complete restart cycle: node1 (baseline boot_id 1f48c3dd, reboot issued, boot_id changed to 9d3b2f29, recovered eth1 address/active Kea service/saved dhcp-server config and client pings); node2 (baseline 0d49f077 -> 5fc8894a, address and pings restored); node3 (baseline 2b3a8d87 -> 66db5faa, address and pings restored); node4 (baseline d5f5239f -> cde59737, playbook/inventory persisted, and a fresh ansible-playbook run against all three managed nodes succeeded end-to-end after re-adding a lost vyos SSH key that VyOS's login-config regeneration had wiped on reboot). These match the fixed after-prepare/after-executor boot-identity cross-check.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-95f7cbb9d5ab4a04\",\"cmd-a68d9e3b9a874402\",\"cmd-b174bed1a6354ce1\",\"cmd-f6be1776a30541d0\",\"cmd-6e913832c6944a31\",\"cmd-4be8c922a06248a0\",\"cmd-326a4960588c4e8d\",\"cmd-1490bf3efcd94f28\",\"cmd-cb64b7cc54084c66\",\"cmd-bb1ed95f84664574\",\"cmd-8705675108354875\",\"cmd-5b26172c155449c5\",\"cmd-4eba0e84b6264df3\",\"cmd-819ed3ed2e6049c3\",\"cmd-dcc5d9da37fe4060\",\"cmd-9d64721c68394974\",\"cmd-3fb4d94a47a84301\",\"cmd-37939d40411547ce\",\"cmd-b14916d478034761\"]}],\"confidence\":0.88,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.78,\"summary\":\"Most of the 51 failed commands were legitimate read-only discovery or failed troubleshooting attempts against VyOS's unusual configuration-session mechanics, with no lasting effect (e.g. cmd-ef1d9c42d3e84417, cmd-1f20b5b9a617408d, cmd-5ae1ce8f11bb4489, cmd-b918b3be367e43b6, cmd-332cf3da2a3e4ffb, cmd-00bd87706e994b98 all resulted in 'Set failed'/no committed changes). Temporary test scripts left in /tmp on node1 during troubleshooting (vyos_test.sh/vyos_test2.sh/vyos_test3.sh/vyos_sg_test.sh/sg_probe.sh) were not explicitly deleted, but the mandatory node1 restart cleared /tmp (tmpfs), and the after-executor temp-file snapshot for node1 shows no leftover test scripts (only the final vyos_dhcp_configure.sh used by the last successful playbook run), so no residue remained. One unnecessary mutation was retained: during diagnosis of the VyOS 'Set failed' issue, the executor ran 'set system name-server 1.1.1.1; commit; save' directly as root (cmd-344ca0b4f69a45ed), adding a top-level system DNS resolver setting unrelated to the DHCP-server task requirement; this was committed and saved to /config/config.boot and there is no evidence it was later removed. This is a bounded, low-risk, non-security-weakening mutation (a single DNS resolver setting) rather than a broad or destructive one. SSH key provisioning to root/vyos/antrieb accounts (e.g. cmd-671cdbe1e7144776, cmd-506b88b4326942c6, cmd-d332d0694a6b4eac) was a necessary prerequisite for Ansible orchestration and is not penalized.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-344ca0b4f69a45ed\",\"cmd-9f94db8df3f3460d\",\"cmd-5ae1ce8f11bb4489\",\"cmd-b918b3be367e43b6\",\"cmd-00bd87706e994b98\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The executor satisfied all material outcomes of the task contract: node1 (VyOS) runs a Kea-backed DHCP server on the shared private network (10.50.50.0/24), and node2/node3 obtain their address on that network from node1 via DHCP instead of remaining unconfigured/static, all implemented and applied through an Ansible playbook run from the control node (node4). The mandatory provider-wide restart-and-recovery protocol was executed and directly evidenced on all four nodes, including a genuine VyOS quirk (login-config regeneration wiping a manually appended SSH key on reboot) that was correctly diagnosed and repaired before final re-verification. Operational hygiene is generally good; the main blemish is one unrelated, low-risk system DNS-resolver setting added during troubleshooting that appears to have persiste
